The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
ret = stmmac_dvr_probe(&pdev->dev, plat_dat, &stmmac_res);
return ret;
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because if `stmmac_dvr_probe` fails, the function returns the error code without calling any exit callback to clean up resources that were initialized earlier. This can lead to resource leaks or an inconsistent state of the device since the initialization effects are not undone.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (ret)
    goto err_exit;

err_exit:
if (plat_dat->exit)
    plat_dat->exit(pdev, plat_dat->bsp_priv);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces an error handling path that checks if `stmmac_dvr_probe` fails. If it does, the code jumps to the `err_exit` label, where it calls the `exit` callback if it exists. This ensures that any resources initialized during the probe are properly cleaned up, preventing resource leaks and maintaining a consistent device state.

